  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have, number of terms in the first group&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;with their mean <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>X</mi></menclose><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;number of terms in whole group is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn></math>&nbsp;and their mean&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>X</mi></menclose><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Variance of first group<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and whole group is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Var</mo><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>250</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow><msup><mfenced><mn>250</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
